# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the two values from your Supabase
# project (Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API). Both are meant to be public:
# the browser key is safe in a bundle because Row Level Security, not the key,
# is what decides who can read what. Never put a *secret* / *service role* key
# here — that one bypasses RLS entirely and must never reach a client.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Supabase renamed this key. Newer projects show it as "publishable" and it
# looks like sb_publishable_...; older ones call it "anon public" and it is a
# JWT starting eyJ... . The app accepts either name, so set whichever one your
# dashboard shows you. If both are set, the publishable one wins.
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_your-key
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...

# Where the app is served from. Used to build invite links, so a partner's
# link opens the right place. Leave unset for local development and for most
# deployments — the app will use the address in the browser's address bar,
# which is correct in both. Set it only if the app is served from a different
# address than the one people open it at.
# VITE_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://couple777.example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The memory-reading endpoint (api/memory-read.ts) — SERVER SIDE ONLY.
#
# These have no VITE_ prefix on purpose: anything prefixed is compiled into the
# browser bundle, and an API key in a bundle is a published API key. Set them
# where the function runs (Vercel → Project Settings → Environment Variables).
#
# Leave them unset and the app reads memories on the device instead.
#
# MEMORY_AI_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# MEMORY_AI_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The date recommender (api/recommend-ideas.ts) — SERVER SIDE ONLY.
#
# It reuses MEMORY_AI_API_KEY above; there is no second key to buy.
#
# The model, though, is its own. Reading a memory is a judgement call about
# someone's evening; ranking is not — eligibility, tiering and every guardrail
# are already settled in code before the model sees anything, so what is left
# is ordering twenty vetted ideas and writing a sentence for each. Sonnet does
# that well and answers sooner, which is the whole point on a screen someone
# is waiting at. Not set here means claude-sonnet-5.
#
# RECOMMEND_AI_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
#
# These two are how the endpoint checks that whoever is asking is signed in.
# Without them it refuses every request, which is the safe way round: an
# unauthenticated endpoint that calls a paid model is a bill with a public URL.
# Both values are the same public ones as the VITE_ pair above — the publishable
# key, never the service-role key, which bypasses RLS and has no business here.
# Only the publishable name is read here: the browser accepts either name
# because a project may show it either way, but this one is the endpoint's own
# variable and is set once.
#
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_your-key
